{
  "an10.218:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.218 ",
  "an10.218:0.2": "21. The Body Born of Deeds ",
  "an10.218:0.3": "Intentional (2nd) ",
  "an10.218:1.1": "“Mendicants, I don’t say that intentional deeds that have been performed and accumulated are eliminated without being experienced. ",
  "an10.218:1.2": "And that may be in this very life, or in the next life, or in some subsequent period. ",
  "an10.218:1.3": "But in any case, there is no making an end of suffering without experiencing intentional deeds that have been performed and accumulated, I say. ",
  "an10.218:2.1": "Now, there are three kinds of corruption and failure of bodily action that have unskillful intention, with suffering as their outcome and result. ",
  "an10.218:2.2": "There are four kinds of corruption and failure of verbal action that have unskillful intention, with suffering as their outcome and result. ",
  "an10.218:2.3": "There are three kinds of corruption and failure of mental action that have unskillful intention, with suffering as their outcome and result. ",
  "an10.218:3.1": "And what are the three kinds of corruption and failure of bodily action? … ",
  "an10.218:3.2": "These are the three kinds of corruption and failure of bodily action. ",
  "an10.218:4.1": "And what are the four kinds of corruption and failure of verbal action? … ",
  "an10.218:4.2": "These are the four kinds of corruption and failure of verbal action. ",
  "an10.218:5.1": "And what are the three kinds of corruption and failure of mental action? 